<main>
<article>
  <h1>Transmission — the molecule is the conduction bridge</h1>
  <p class="page-meta">Zero-bias T(E), three-way comparison, and the real-space channel</p>

  <h2>Goal</h2>
  <p>Show whether current flows <em>through</em> the molecule, and through which channel.</p>

  <h2>Method</h2>
  <p>TranSIESTA / TBtrans, vdW-DF2, ~220-atom device, electrode k = 100, η = 0.005 eV.
     $T(E)$ via sisl from <code>trans.TBT.nc</code>; eigenchannel $|\psi|^2$ isosurface at $E_F$.</p>

  <h2>Result</h2>
  <p>The three-way comparison is the central evidence:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>System</th><th>$T(E_F)$</th><th>Reading</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Pristine VSe₃</td><td>0.68</td><td>reference (continuous chain)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Heterojunction</td><td>0.35</td><td>conducts through the molecule</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Disconnected</td><td>0</td><td>molecule removed → no conduction</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <figure>
    <img src="figures/te-3way.png" alt="Three-way transmission">
    <figcaption><strong>Fig. 1.</strong> $T(E)$ — with molecule (green) / pristine (blue) /
      disconnected (red, on the floor). Removing the molecule kills conduction.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>
    Removing the molecule drops $T(E_F)$ to zero, so the molecule is the <strong>sole conduction
    bridge</strong>. The transmitting eigenchannel crosses it with $\tau_0 \approx 1$ (Fig. 2);
    frontier resonances sit at −0.065 / +0.175 eV, straddling $E_F$. k-grid (4→100) and η are
    converged ($T(E_F)$ shifts ~0.3%).
  </p>
  <figure>
    <img src="figures/eigenchannel-EF.png" alt="Eigenchannel isosurface at E_F">
    <figcaption><strong>Fig. 2.</strong> $|\psi|^2$ of the transmitting eigenchannel (EC₀,
      $\tau\approx1$) at $E_F$: runs through both leads, concentrates on the molecule.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Discussion</h2>
  <p>
    Conduction is resonant because the PBE/vdW-DF molecular resonance sits on $E_F$. Whether it
    stays resonant under a corrected gap is the open question driving the
    <a href="../../methods/index.html">B3LYP level correction</a>; the finite-bias I–V is the
    remaining deliverable.
  </p>
</article>
